Keep Alive Time in {{units}} defines the maximum wait time after which a packet has to be sent to the MQTT broker (see {{bibref|MQTT311|section 3.1}}, {{bibref|MQTT311|section 3.1.2.10}}) or {{bibref|MQTT50|section 3.1.2.10}}). If no regular packet can be sent a MQTT PINGREQ packet is sent.
A value of zero (0) means no keep alive packets are sent and the MQTT client is not disconnected by the server.
